      "assessment": {
        "nobel_worthiness": "Quantum error correction identified how fragile quantum information can be protected, changing the physical prospects for scalable quantum computation.",
        "attribution": "Shor, Steane, and Kitaev made distinct foundational contributions to codes, fault tolerance, and topological protection.",
        "maturity": "Core principles are firmly established and increasingly demonstrated in hardware, though fully fault-tolerant machines remain ahead.",
        "uncertainties": [
