        "Juan Ignacio Cirac",
        "Peter Zoller",
        "Rainer Blatt"
      ],
      "assessment": {
        "nobel_worthiness": "Atomic quantum processing and simulation turned controllable many-body quantum systems into a general experimental science.",
        "attribution": "Cirac and Zoller provided pivotal architectures and protocols, with Blatt central to their experimental realization.",
        "maturity": "The field has delivered reproducible processors, simulators, and precision tests over decades.",
        "uncertainties": [
          "The candidate's broad scope overlaps substantially with trapped-ion quantum computation."
