      "assessment": {
        "nobel_worthiness": "The quantum spin Hall effect and topological-insulator framework revealed a new robust class of electronic quantum matter.",
        "attribution": "Kane and Mele supplied the foundational theory, and Molenkamp led a decisive experimental observation.",
        "maturity": "The physics has been independently confirmed and has reshaped condensed-matter research.",
        "uncertainties": [
          "Several later experimental and theoretical contributors have strong claims to recognition."
